course: dictionary
lesson: 15755
title: Triplets: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A triplet is one of three babies born to the same mother at the same time. Words around a word can give you clues. «Mum had triplets, so the hospital had three new babies to care for that day.» The clues are three and babies, so triplets must mean three children born together.
explain: The word also means a group of three things. «The shop sold a triplet of red, blue and green pens.» Here the clue is three pens of different colours, so a triplet is a set of three that go together.
explain: Maths and music use triplets too. The numbers 3, 4 and 5 form a Pythagorean triplet, because 3² + 4² = 5². In music, a triplet is three notes played in the time usually taken by two, which gives a bouncy rhythm.
fact: A triplet is one of three children born to the same mother at the same time.
fact: «Triplets» can also mean a group of three things that go together.
fact: «Identical triplets» look very alike, so they can be hard to tell apart.
fact: A Pythagorean triplet such as 3, 4, 5 fits a right-angled triangle: 3² + 4² = 5².
fact: In music, a triplet is three notes played in the time usually taken by two.
exercise: Mum had triplets, so there were three new babies at once. What is a triplet here? | A baby who is very quiet | *One of three children born to the same mother at the same time | Two babies born on different days | A type of pram
exercise: «The shop sold a triplet of red, blue and green pens.» What does triplet mean in this sentence? | A kind of pencil case | Two pens in a box | A pen that writes in three colours | *A group of three things
exercise: Which set of numbers is a Pythagorean triplet? | 1, 2, 3 | 4, 4, 4 | 2, 5, 8 | *3, 4, 5
test: «The triplets wore matching yellow jumpers.» Who are the triplets? | A kind of jumper | Two adults at a party | *Three children born together | One baby with a twin
test: In music, what is a triplet? | One long held note | Two notes played very loudly | *Three notes played in the time usually taken by two | A song with four verses
exam: «Identical triplets look so alike that even their teacher finds them hard to tell apart.» Why is it hard? | *Because the triplets look very alike | Because the teacher cannot see well | Because triplets are always different sizes | Because triplets never go to school
